  "content": {
    "id": "p132-task49-52",
    "type": "question",
    "label": null,
    "prompt": "Determine whether the following functions are odd, even, or neither.",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p132-task49-52-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$f(x)=\\dfrac{2^{2x}+1}{2^x}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": {
            "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
            "version": 1,
            "blocks": [
              {
                "id": "p132-q49-short-result",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Even.",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "p132-q49-short-method",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Replacing ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "x",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": " by ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "-x",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": " exchanges the terms in ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "2^x+2^{-x}",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": ".",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          "worked": "The domain is $\\mathbb{R}$. Simplifying and substituting gives\n$$\\begin{align*}\nf(x)&=2^x+2^{-x}\\\\\nf(-x)&=2^{-x}+2^x\\\\\nf(-x)&=f(x).\n\\end{align*}$$\nTherefore, $f$ is even.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 36
      },
      {
        "id": "p132-task49-52-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$f(x)=\\dfrac{1}{1+2^x}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": {
            "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
            "version": 1,
            "blocks": [
              {
                "id": "p132-q50-short-result",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Neither.",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "p132-q50-short-method",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "f(1)=\\frac13",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": " and ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "f(-1)=\\frac23",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": ", so both symmetry tests fail.",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          "worked": "The domain is $\\mathbb{R}$ because $1+2^x>0$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\nf(-x)&=\\frac{1}{1+2^{-x}}\\\\\nf(-x)&=\\frac{2^x}{1+2^x}.\n\\end{align*}$$\nIn particular,\n$$\\begin{align*}\nf(1)&=\\frac13\\\\\nf(-1)&=\\frac23.\n\\end{align*}$$\nSince $f(-1)\\ne f(1)$ and $f(-1)\\ne-f(1)$, $f$ is neither even nor odd.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 38
      },
      {
        "id": "p132-task49-52-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$f(x)=\\dfrac{2^x-2^{-x}}{2^x+2^{-x}}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": {
            "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
            "version": 1,
            "blocks": [
              {
                "id": "p132-q51-short-result",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Odd.",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "p132-q51-short-method",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Replacing ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "x",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": " by ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "-x",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": " changes only the numerator’s sign.",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          "worked": "The domain is $\\mathbb{R}$ because $2^x+2^{-x}>0$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\nf(-x)&=\\frac{2^{-x}-2^x}{2^{-x}+2^x}\\\\\nf(-x)&=-\\frac{2^x-2^{-x}}{2^x+2^{-x}}\\\\\nf(-x)&=-f(x).\n\\end{align*}$$\nTherefore, $f$ is odd.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 38
      },
      {
        "id": "p132-task49-52-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$f(x)=\\dfrac{x}{2^x-2^{-x}}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": {
            "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
            "version": 1,
            "blocks": [
              {
                "id": "p132-q52-short-result",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Even, with ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "x\\ne0",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": ".",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "p132-q52-short-method",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Both numerator and denominator change sign under ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "x\\mapsto-x",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": ".",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          "worked": "The denominator is zero only when $x=0$. Thus the domain is $\\mathbb{R}\\setminus\\{0\\}$, which is symmetric about $0$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\nf(-x)&=\\frac{-x}{2^{-x}-2^x}\\\\\nf(-x)&=\\frac{x}{2^x-2^{-x}}\\\\\nf(-x)&=f(x).\n\\end{align*}$$\nTherefore, $f$ is even on its domain, $x\\ne0$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 38
      }
    ]
